From: immortalwrt-x86-fm350-pcie <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: t7xx: initialize MAC header for raw IP RX

T7xx receives raw IP packets in freshly allocated skbs and passes them to
napi_gro_receive() without initializing mac_header. The allocation leaves
mac_header at the unset value, 0xffff, while GRO and the receive core derive
mac_len from the difference between network_header and mac_header.

With 128 bytes of RX headroom this produces a bogus mac_len of 129. An
ingress mirred redirect to an IFB then calls skb_push_rcsum() with that
length, moving data one byte before head and triggering skb_under_panic.

Reset the MAC header to the start of the raw IP packet before entering GRO.
The network header is at the same position, so the derived MAC length is
zero. This fixes the header metadata without disabling GRO, fraglist GRO,
checksum offload, or SQM ingress shaping.

This is a local fix, not an upstream backport.

---
 drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/t7xx/t7xx_netdev.c
@@ -432,6 +432,9 @@ static void t7xx_ccmni_recv_skb(struct t7xx_ccmni_ctrl *ccmni_ctlb, struct sk_buff
 	else
 		skb->protocol = htons(ETH_P_IP);
 
+	/* The modem supplies raw IP packets without a MAC header. */
+	skb_reset_mac_header(skb);
+
 	skb_len = skb->len;
 	napi_gro_receive(napi, skb);
 	net_dev->stats.rx_packets++;
